of credit, student loans, loans on savings accounts, overdraft line of credit, and other consumer loans. In addition, the company invests in mortgage-backed securities, securities issued by the U.S. government and agencies, corporate securities, and other investments; and provides bankcard services, trust and asset management products and services, deposit account services, sales of loans and investments, bank owned life insurance and commercial loan swap income. The company was founded in 1902 and is headquartered in Toms River, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher D. Maher | CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 898 people. Revenue per employee of $451K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $89K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["OceanFirst Financial Corp. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.8B market cap on $405M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +16% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $80M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.23\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 100% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.0663104257340992},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.0M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2027783.14},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["28 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"OceanFirst Financial (OCFC) After Earnings And A Fresh Dividend Looks Undervalued","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-ocfc/oceanfirst-financial/news/oceanfirst-financial-ocfc-after-earnings-and-a-fresh-dividen","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp